{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815578-fear-united-vampires-with-beast-blood","id":815578,"title":"Fear United: Vampires with Beast blood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-24T11:11:03-08:00","id":815578,"title":"Fear United: Vampires with Beast blood","content":"So considering Unnatural Affinity, Beasts' affinity with fears and nightmares, their mythology's similarity to the Circle and the Nightmare discipline, I was wondering what kind of merits and devotions could be brought from this.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking there could be a merit where if you have partaken in Beasts' blood lately, you wold gain bonus dice for Nightmare disciplines.<br /> <br /> Any other ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:53:12-08:00","id":815600,"title":"","content":"Isn't there an innate component of Beast blood that enhances supernaturals that consume it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T12:50:47-08:00","id":815636,"title":"","content":"Beast blood or participation could do funky things to Cr\u00faac Rites. Nightmare Devotions that require you to have partaken of Beast blood. A Nosferatu Bloodline born from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T21:19:37-08:00","id":815888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815578-fear-united-vampires-with-beast-blood?p=815600#post815600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there an innate component of Beast blood that enhances supernaturals that consume it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really, it's an innate component of the beast, not the blood itself, or else the beast wouldn't have to spend willpower on it.<br /> <br /> Plus you know, I don't see the power being weakened just because the beast got a blood transfusion.<br /> <br /> Anyway, ideas for ways vampires might get merits or devotions based on beasts-<br /> <br /> There's already a few bloodlines that can control the environment around them, so how about some lair like devotions?<br /> <br /> In mythologies there's a devotion for vampires entering dreams, a vampire &quot;learning&quot; that from a beast seems reasonable. <br /> <br /> Or how about a vampire learning how to manifest their beast in a beast like fashion? Maybe a protean/nightmare devotion? <br /> <br /> In blood sorcery there's a protean merit for getting ones beast to allow them to transform into a mythological creature, that's very beast like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 01-25-2016, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T10:57:30-08:00","id":816991,"title":"","content":"My idea is that taking Vitae is more than just drinking blood, it also has a spiritual component. So, here's my suggestion:<br /> <br /> <b>Unnatural Affinity: Beasts:</b> The Kindred can draw sustenance from the Begotten, and even more, may draw on a portion of the eldritch power found within the tiny bit of blood and soul that they take from the Beast. The Vampire gains a +1 bonuns to all rolls in relation to the Nightmare Discipline, except resisting. Based on ST discretion, this bonus may extend to Lashing out with the Monstrous Beast or rolls related to Cruac rituals.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Beast calls to Beast. You suffer a -1 bonus to resist Frenzy.<br /> Both benefit and drawback last ffor a number of nights equal to the points of Vitae taken from the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:54:22-08:00","id":818528,"title":"","content":"I think that Cruac Rituals in general might react weirdly to beast blood. And I mean that in the priestess going &quot;What the hell just happened?&quot; soft of way. I can picture that a beasts family might add some other weird side effects like Anakim blood might cause a massive surge of power making the ritual harder to control but granting a potency bonus for every 10 rolled. An Eshmaki might make the ritual more dangerous causing it to cripple or maim the target, or apply a tilt of some kind for the duration of the ritual. A Makara grant a penalty the same as it's birthright but the duration of the ritual. The Namtaru's blood weakens the composure of the target and causes them to treat their composure as one less for the duration of the effect. The Blood of an Ugulu causes the target to gain the guilty and the intoxicated conditions as they feel extreme vertigo and the feeling that someone else knows their sins these cannot be resolved until the duration of the ritual has ended.<br /> <br /> Though if a dramatic failure occurs then the caster takes the brunt of the power of the beasts vitae, and this double edged sword cuts them. The Anakim power causes bashing damage equal to every 1, 2 or 3 rolled.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}